WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.840
The Witcher offers some clues as to its chronology
for fans who are paying close attention.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.200
With work, you can piece more or less the
entire timeline together.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.000
There are still some questions and ambiguities,
but the overall picture works just fine.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.280
Here's what you need to know.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.960
Viewers don't see the earliest scenes in The
Witcher until the season's final episode.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:24.300
Through Geralt's flashbacks, we meet his biological
mother, Visenna, and watch as she abandons

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:29.280
Geralt at Kaer Morhen, where he meets his
mentor Vesemir and begins his witcher training.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:34.079
In an interview, The Witcher showrunner Lauren
Schmidt Hissrich revealed that Geralt is already

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.020
100 years old by the time viewers meet him
in the first episode.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.120
That means that young Geralt's scenes must've
happened at the very beginning of The Witcher

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:41.620
timeline.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:47.240
Of The Witcher's three main timelines, Yennefer's
origin story comes first.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:52.020
Yennefer looks fairly young when Tissaia buys
her from her father in episode two, and all

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:55.420
of Yennefer's early days happen before the
rest of the main plot.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:59.400
We don't know how long Yennefer spends at
school, but it doesn't seem like much.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:04.070
Hunchback Yennefer, who should age like a
normal human, doesn't show many physical changes

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:04.960
during her studies.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:10.380
However, according to Hissrich, Yennefer's
story in season one spans about 70 years.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:15.190
After ascending, Yennefer spends 30 years
in the court at Aedirn, and another 10 or

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:18.760
so kicking around as an independent sorceress
before the Battle of Sodden.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:21.140
That leaves 30 years unaccounted for.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:25.720
Either Hissrich had her numbers wrong, or
Yennefer trains at Aretuza for a lot longer

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:26.440
than it seems.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:29.640
Geralt's first three adventures take place
next.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.680
It's not clear exactly how long it takes Geralt
to become known as the Butcher of Blaviken

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:37.620
or how long it took Jaskier to make Geralt
famous.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:42.300
Given that Geralt's entire story in season
one is about 20 years long, and that 12 years

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:47.531
pass between Geralt's two visits to Cintra,
an eight-year period between episode one and

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.020
episode four makes sense.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:54.100
We can also surmise that Geralt's battle with
the striga in episode three takes place about

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.300
30 years after Yennefer's transformation.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:02.100
At the sorceror's ball in Yennefer's timeline,
King Foltest of Temeria can be seen pestering

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:05.680
his sister Adda, and the future monarch looks
to be around 10 years old.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:10.020
When Geralt meets him, Foltest is in his 40s,
and Adda has been dead for years.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.680
Yennefer and Geralt's stories in episode four
seem to happen at around the same time.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:19.000
Yennefer claims that she's been at Aedirn
for three decades before she decides to strike

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:22.849
out on her own, and that's about how much
time has passed for Foltest in Geralt's timeline

00:02:22.849 --> 00:02:23.760
in episode three.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:28.680
Further, Geralt's reputation is firmly established
by the time that he first enters Queen Calanthe's

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:29.180
court.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:32.880
This is the first episode that makes it crystal
clear that we're following three separate

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:33.380
timelines.

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:38.520
In the episode, Nilfgaard is a joke, and Ciri's
mother is newly pregnant.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:43.850
In the first episode, though, Calanthe and
Eist are married, Ciri is 12 years old, and

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:45.360
Nilfgaard is a mighty military force.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:51.380
In "Bottled Appetites," the star-crossed lovers
Geralt and Yennefer meet for the very first

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.360
time, courtesy of a djinn in a bottle.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:57.951
Enough time passes between "Bottled Appetites"
and "Rare Species" for Geralt and Yennefer

00:02:57.960 --> 00:02:59.640
to build up quite a bit of history.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:03.859
Their bickering references numerous encounters
beyond the one we've already seen, and they

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:05.780
seem to have spent quite a bit of time together.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:10.120
Yennefer and Jaskier know each other pretty
well at this point, too, and they don't seem

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:10.760
to get along.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.240
"witchers are bound to run into monsters

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:13.740
eventually."

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:15.740
"Jaskier."

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:16.920
"Yennefer."

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.000
"The crow's feet are new."

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:20.220
Cintra falls

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.420
Finally, Ciri's story begins brings the three
timelines together with the collapse of Cintra.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:28.780
In the leadup to Nilfgaard's attack, Yennefer
joins the Brotherhood of Sorcerers to discuss

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:33.389
the impending invasion, while Geralt goes
directly to Cintra to try to rescue Ciri.

00:03:33.389 --> 00:03:37.340
In fact, Geralt was in Cintra when Ciri fled
the city.

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:41.260
Unfortunately, Calanthe had locked him in
a dungeon to keep him from running off with

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:41.760
Ciri.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:46.360
At any rate, Ciri's storyline in episode one
and Geralt and Yennefer's plots in episode

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:47.800
seven happen at the same time.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.840
According to Hissrich, Ciri's story in The
Witcher's first season unfolds over the course

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:53.680
of a couple of weeks.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:59.359
Ciri meets Dara shortly after escaping Cintra,
and only spends a little bit of time in the

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.720
refugee camp before Nilfgaard attacks.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:05.000
A few days later, she enters Brokilon Forest.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:10.400
After a few nights in Brokilon, the doppler,
disguised as Mousesack, takes Ciri and Dara

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:10.900
away.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:14.200
Ciri discovers the deception and frees herself
soon afterwards.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:16.000
From there, Ciri fends for herself.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.780
She tries to pawn off her jewelry for cash,
and is ultimately offered a home by a kindly

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:22.280
woman with a house in the woods.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:27.540
All of this unfolds in the time between Geralt's
second visit to Cintra in episode seven and

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:30.240
his arrival at the former refugee camp in
episode eight.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:34.780
By the beginning of episode eight, "Much More,"
all three timelines are in sync.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:39.530
While Yennefer and her fellow sorcerers are
fighting Nilfgaard at Sodden, Geralt is fighting

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:44.160
for his life on the back of a merchant's cart,
and Ciri is waiting in a cabin with the merchant's

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:44.660
wife.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:48.000
All of this happens about a week after Ciri
fled the refugee camp.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:52.200
When Geralt first meets the merchant, the
man is cleaning up the bodies the Nilfgaardian

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.300
army left behind.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.000
The episode also takes place over a couple
of days.

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:59.620
The sorcerers arrive at Sodden and prep their
defenses in the daytime.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:04.440
The ensuing battle begins at night, takes
the whole next day, and ends just before dawn.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:08.040
The morning after the battle is when Geralt
and Ciri meet for the first time.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:12.580
Yennefer disappears after using a ton of magic
to channel fire at the Nilfgaardian army,

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.780
but she's probably not gone for good.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:18.360
As the season ends, Yennefer is the one everyone's
talking about.

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:19.480
"Who is Yennefer?"

